# [CORE](../wg/core.html)

## Summary

The Constrained RESTful Environments (CoRE) Working Group met at IETF 127. The session covered administration and document status updates, progress on core protocol extensions (CoAP over BP, CoRECONF/COMI, Observe Multicast Notifications, OSCORE key update and proxies), and several individual proposals addressing post-quantum security, OSCORE option obfuscation, Oblivious CoAP, a new 2.06 No Content response code, diagnostic message notation, and SID file extensions. Multiple active drafts are approaching Working Group Last Call (WGLC), and plans were made to stagger reviews to manage community bandwidth.

---

## Key Discussion Points

### Administration and Document Status
* **Presented by:** Marco Tiloca, Jaime Jiménez, Carsten Bormann
* **Slides:** [Chairs' slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-core-chairs-slides-01)
* RFC 9997 has been published as Proposed Standard. Several documents (`draft-ietf-core-href`, etc.) are in final RFC Editor review or blocked only by cluster references.
* Post-WGLC documents (`draft-ietf-core-yang-cbor` and `draft-ietf-core-conditional-attributes`) are being prepared for publication requests by their respective shepherds.
* A brief update was provided on hackathon projects covering CoAP over BP, Oblivious CoAP, and AI-agent-driven interoperability testing.

### Constrained Application Protocol (CoAP) over Bundle Protocol (BP)
* **Draft:** `draft-ietf-core-coap-bp`
* **Presented by:** Anna Calveras
* **Slides:** [CoAP over BP](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-core-coap-over-bp-00)
* Changes in version -05 focus exclusively on the 3-element `ipn` URI scheme using `.ipn.alt` suffix, dropping the DTN scheme from scope to avoid DNS dependencies.
* Corrected calculations for bundle lifetime during message aggregation ($bundle\_lifetime = change\_lifetime - max\_aggregation\_delay$) and noted that aggregation requires an increased `NSTART` value.
* Updated block-wise non-timeout calculations following RFC 9177.
* Practical implementations and hackathon demo results were reported; authors consider the draft approaching WGLC readiness.

### CoAP Management Interface (CORECONF)
* **Draft:** `draft-ietf-core-comi` (also addressing `draft-ietf-core-yang-metadata`)
* **Presented by:** Carsten Bormann, Alexander Pelov
* **Slides:** [CoRECONF](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-core-coreconf-00)
* **YANG-CBOR SID Workflows:** Carsten Bormann reported on automated toolchains for designated expert and IANA interaction during SID allocations, processing batches of YANG modules using a `pyang 2.7.1` patch.
* **Appendix D Resolution:**
  1. *Mandatory-to-Implement (MTI) Security:* Agreed that no single MTI security mechanism (DTLS vs OSCORE vs Layer 2) fits all deployment models. The specification will describe available options without mandating a single MTI.
  2. *SIDs in URI Paths:* Agreed to maintain the current separation (SIDs in fetch payloads) and defer mixing SIDs into URI path segments to future work.
  3. *Resource Discovery:* Acknowledged as useful but deferred to separate mechanisms (e.g., link-format metadata).
* The authors plan to submit draft `-23` before Thanksgiving to trigger a Working Group Last Call.

